MISTAKES = [
 'Mixing up the names: <b>Sentila</b> is the daughter who wants to learn pot making, <b>Arenla</b> is her skilled mother, and <b>Onula</b> is the kind older woman who guides her. Do not call the mother Onula.',
 "Saying Arenla refused out of dislike for her daughter. She wished to spare Sentila a tiring, poorly paid craft; the elders' view was that skills belong to the community and must be passed on.",
 "In 'Quality', saying Mr Gessler failed because his boots were poor. His business suffered because bigger firms advertised while he stayed faithful to <b>hand-made quality</b>; the story contrasts honest craft with commerce.",
 "Giving the meaning of 'vocation' as a holiday or hobby. It means an occupation one is suited to; link it to the <b>dignity of labour</b> in the poems.",
 "Spelling and usage slips: <i>skilful</i> (one 'l' in British spelling); 'spoke <b>to</b> Sentila', not 'spoke on'. Plural of boot is <i>boots</i>.",
 "Writing one story's facts under the other's title. Keep the two prose pieces separate: a village potter and a bootmaker, and mention a poem only when the question names it.",
]
